                "en": "The reasoning depends on the woman’s own knowledge: if she were not sure of her purity, she would examine herself. On this explanation, the husband’s request therefore suffices for the examination Shmuel discussed. Rashi immediately adds that his mind hesitates. He does not explain the cause of that hesitation here, so the explanation must not be presented as an unqualified resolution."
